The requirements still live in two prereq blocks in dist.ini:

    [Prereqs]
    Path::Tiny = 0

    [Prereqs / TestRequires]
    Test::More = 0.98

The house rule is that requirements live in a cpanfile, not in dist.ini prereq blocks. The [@Author::GETTY] bundle adds the Prereqs::FromCPANfile plugin, so dzil reads the cpanfile and the dist.ini blocks are a second source of truth for the same two requirements.

Work:
- create cpanfile with the runtime requirement requires Path::Tiny,; (unpinned, no version) and an on test => sub { requires Test::More, 0.98; }; phase block at the end
- remove both prereq blocks from dist.ini, so each requirement exists in exactly one place
- verify with dzil listdeps --author that Path::Tiny is still a runtime requirement and Test::More a test requirement

House format for the cpanfile: alphabetical, requires Module::Name, with the version as the minimum (never >=), phase blocks at the end.

